          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            consists of a collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            each having a single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            as source or input, and a single object as target or output, together with laws for composition and identity obeying associativity and identity axioms. A
            %em multicategory
            is like a category, except that one allows multiple inputs and a single output.
          %p
            Another term for
            %em multicategory
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                coloured
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_components In components
          %p
            A
            %strong multicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            consists of
          %ul
            %li
              A collection of
              = succeed "," do
                %em objects
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
            %li
              A collection of
              = succeed "," do
                %em multimorphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_1
            %li
              A source map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s: C_1 \to (C_0)*
              to the collection of finite, possibly empty
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/list"} list
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C_0)*
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+monoid"} free monoid
              generated by
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_0
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi t
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t: C_1 \to C_0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: c_1, \ldots, c_n \to c
              to indicate the source and target of a multimorphism
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %li
              Identity and composition laws. The identity law is a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_{-}: C_0 \to C_1
              where
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %mi c
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_c: c \to c
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi c
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: c_1, \ldots, c_n \to c
              together with an
              = succeed "-tuple" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mi i
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi c
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle f_i: \vec{c}_i \to c_i: i = 1, \ldots, n \rangle
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \circ (f_1, \ldots, f_n): \vec{c}_1, \ldots, \vec{c}_n \to c
              %p where the source is obtained by concatenating lists in the evident way.
          %p
            These operations are subject to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associativity"} associativity
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
            axioms which the reader can probably figure out, but see for example (
            %a{:href => "#Leinster"}> Leinster, page 35 ff.
            ), for details.
          %p
            Many people (especially non-category theorists) use the word
            %em multicategory
            or the word
            %em
              colored
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            to mean what we would call a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+multicategory"} symmetric multicategory
            \/
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operad"} symmetric operad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_n
            on the multimorphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c_1, \ldots, c_n \to c
            such that the composition is equivariant with respect to these actions.
          %h3#in_terms_of_cartesian_monads In terms of cartesian monads
          %p
            An efficient abstract method for defining multicategories and related structures is through the formalism of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monads"} cartesian monads
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+monoid"} free monoid
            monad
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo *
                    %mo :
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)*: Set \to Set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategory"} generalized multicategory
          %p
            We summarize here how the theory applies to the case of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monad"} cartesian monad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            on a category with
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullbacks"} pullbacks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategory"} generalized multicategory
            for the fully general context.
          %ul
            %li
              First, a
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                \-span
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/span"} span
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
              to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 1
                      %mi P
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi p
                            %mn 2
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X \stackrel{p_1}{\leftarrow} P \stackrel{p_2}{\to} Y
              %p
                A
                = succeed "-span" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %mi X
                        %mi ⇸
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p: X &amp;#8696; Y
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is the free monoid monad on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            = succeed "-span" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to itself is called a
            %em multigraph
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                \-spans are the 1-cells of a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
                = succeed "-spans" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ,
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mi ⇸
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e, f: X &amp;#8696; Y
                is a 2-cell between ordinary spans from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X
                to
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                = succeed "-spans" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo :
                      %mi X
                      %mi ⇸
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e: X &amp;#8696; Y
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mi Y
                        %mi ⇸
                        %mi Z
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: Y &amp;#8696; Z
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %mi m
                          %mi X
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mn 2
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %msub
                            %mi e
                            %mn 1
                      %mi T
                      %mi E
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %msub
                            %mi e
                            %mn 2
                      %mi T
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mi Y
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 1
                      %mi F
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mn 2
                      %mi Z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (T X \stackrel{m X}{\leftarrow} T^2 X \stackrel{T e_1}{\leftarrow} T E \stackrel{T e_2}{\to} T Y) \circ (T Y \stackrel{f_1}{\leftarrow} F \stackrel{f_2}{\to} Z)
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi T
                        %mn 2
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m: T^2 \to T
                is the monad multiplication. The identity
                = succeed "-span" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                to itself is the span
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mrow
                          %mi u
                          %mi X
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mn 1
                            %mi X
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T X \stackrel{u X}{\leftarrow} X \stackrel{1_X}{\to} X
              %p
                where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi u
                      %mo :
                      %mi I
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u: I \to T
                is the monad unit. The verification of the bicategory axioms uses the cartesianness of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                in concert with the corresponding axioms on the bicategory of spans.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                  \-multicategory
                is defined to be a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
                in the bicategory of
                = succeed "-spans." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is the free monoid monad on sets, then a
            = succeed "-multicategory" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategory"} generalized multicategory
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_operads Relation to operads
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonpermutative+operad"} nonpermutative
            (or Stasheff-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            may be defined as an ordinary multicategory with exactly one object. Likewise, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operad"} symmetric operad
            in any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is equivalent to a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            multicategory with one object.
          %p
            More generally, the notion of
            %em
              multi-colored
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/planar+operad"} planar operad
            is equivalent to that of multicategory, and the notion of
            %em
              multi-colored
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+operad"} symmetric operad
            is equivalent to that of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+multicategory"} symmetric multicategory
          %p
            Fully generally, for each cartesian monad
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-operad," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-multicategory" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-span" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mi ⇸
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 &amp;#8696; 1
          %p
            For example, in Batanin’s approach to (weak)
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-category"} categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globular+operad"} globular operad
            is a
            = succeed "-operad," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is the free (strict)
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+omega-category"} category
            monad on the category of
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globular+set"} globular set
          %p
            Ordinary (permutative/symmetric) operads, and their generalization to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+multicategory"} symmetric multicategories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategories"} generalized multicategories
          %h3#relation_to_monoidal_categories Relation to monoidal categories
          %p
            There is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-adjunction"} 2-adjunction
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            of multicategories and the 2-category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+monoidal+categories"} strict monoidal categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+monoidal+functors"} strict monoidal functors
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+natural+transformations"} monoidal natural transformations
