            The left adjoint sends a multicategory to its
            = succeed "." do
              %strong monoidal envelope
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1, \ldots, A_n \to B
            given by morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_1 \otimes \cdots \otimes A_n \to B
            (which is a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+multicategory"} representable multicategory
          %p
            The right adjoint is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                locally fully faithful
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/locally+fully+faithful"} ?
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functors"} lax monoidal functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monadic"} 2-monadic
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+2-adjunction"} lax-idempotent
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful"} full and faithful
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                  %mo →
                  %mi UFM
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \to UFM
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful"} fully faithful
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudoalgebras"} pseudoalgebras
            for the induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
            are precisely the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+multicategories"} representable multicategories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
          %p
            The adjunction is also
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonadic"} comonadic
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nuclear+adjunction"} nuclear adjunction
          %p
            There is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful"} fully faithful
            2-functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi StrMonCat
                    %mi l
                  %mo →
                  %mi Multicat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} StrMonCat_l \to Multicat
            (abstractly, this is the forgetful functor from the 2-category of
            %span.newWikiWord
              strict algebras
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/strict+algebras"} ?
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+morphisms"} lax morphisms
            for the induced 2-monad).
          %p
            For details on some of this material see (
            %a{:href => "Hermida2000"}> Hermida 2000
            ).
          %h3#exponentiability Exponentiability
          %p
            A multicategory is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponentiable+object"} exponentiable
            if and only if it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/promonoidal+category"} promonoidal
            (Proposition 2.8 of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Pisani14"} Pisani 2014
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+multicategories"} representable multicategories
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+multicategories"} sequential multicategories
            are exponentiable. This gives an abstract construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
            tensor product on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C, D]
            for any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/promonoidal+category"} promonoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi D
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D^C
          %h2#examples_and_special_cases Examples and special cases
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutative+categories"} permutative categories
              with multi-linear functors between them form a multicategory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PermCat"} PermCat
          %p
            See also the examples at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multimorphism"} multimorphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multifunctor"} multifunctor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiactegory"}> multiactegory
                , the appropriate notion of
                %em action
                of a multicategory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+of+multicategories"}> fibration of multicategories
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opfibration+of+multicategories"} opfibration of multicategories
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polycategory"} polycategory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/properad"} properad
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+of+multicategories"} fibration of multicategories
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+multicategory"} symmetric multicategory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+multicategory"} cartesian multicategory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+multicategory"} sequential multicategory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategory"}> generalized multicategory
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration+of+multicategories"} fibration of multicategories
          %h2#references References
          %p Multicategories were introduced in:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Lambek"}> Joachim Lambek
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Deductive systems and categories II. Standard constructions and closed categories
          %p and developed further in:
          %ul
            %li
              Joachim Lambek,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Multicategories revisited
          %p
            Hermida constructed a monadic 2-adjunction between the 2-category of nonsymmetric colored operads in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Set
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Set, \times)
            (which he calls
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategories"} multicategories
          %ul#Hermida
            %li#Hermida2000
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Hermida"}> Claudio Hermida
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Representable multicategories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0001870899918777/"} pdf
            %li
              %p
